         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Web::Simple versions before 0.036 for Perl do not escape values interpolated into double-quoted strings in HTML::Tags output.\n\nUnder use HTML::Tags or use XML::Tags, a double-quoted string literal becomes a StringThing object that holds each interpolated value as a separate part. The escaping step passes such objects through, and stringify joins their interpolated parts as is. A value passed on its own, as in <p>, $value, </p>, is entity-escaped, but the same value in \"Hello $value\" is not.\n\nAn attacker who controls a value that an application interpolates into a double-quoted string can inject script into the generated page.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
